<title>BELGIUM: Belgian yr/yr inflation 2.36 pct in November.</title>
<headline>Belgian yr/yr inflation 2.36 pct in November.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Economic Affairs Ministry released the following data on inflation -</p>
<p>    BELGIAN CONSUMER PRICES     Nov 1996   Oct 1996   Nov 1995</p>
<p>    Index (base 100=1988)	 123.57     123.38     120.72</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	 0.15	 0.29	 0.25</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change (in pct)	   2.36	 2.46	 1.47</p>
<p>    Health index *		  121.12     121.00</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	 0.10	 0.19</p>
<p>NOTE - * excludes unhealthy products such as tobacco, alcohol and petrol, is used for inflation adjustments of rents and wages.</p>
<p>The ministry said price rises were mainly seen for foreign travel and fresh fruit, while for liquid fuels and fresh vegetables lower prices were recorded.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
